[step] Required graphic relief: the white frame, mark, lettering and QR rise 0.48 mm above the black face, over their 0.72 mm embedded colour volume. This is the specified two-layer relief of the First Edition artwork; the full plate has CAD review, with its printed artwork unqualified.
alternatives: Flush inlay removes the raised edge; a larger rise adds an unnecessary taller edge to the same graphic.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/nameplate/nameplate-001.step
click: x=-38.930 y=3.840 z=-14.333

[sliver] Required graphic outlines: these strips are the 0.48 mm-high sides of the frame, divider, QR and letter outlines, plus the divider's 0.42 mm-wide front. Their dimensions define the approved fine frame and type rather than an incidental junction between mechanical features.
alternatives: Wider frame and divider strokes change the requested light border. Removing the raised side faces requires flush artwork; larger letterforms spend the balanced spacing to the identification lines and QR.
