[ceiling] Wrong print-axis classification: these are the divider and frame end edges. The nameplate beds on its flat back at Y0 with CAD +Y upward (PRINT_TILT_X=90), while the ceiling finder only applies PRINT_UP to CAD Z. These edges stand vertically during the face-up print; they are not unsupported print-down ceilings. Reported to Derek.
alternatives: Evaluate ceiling normals and height in the complete print pose, as the ledge finder already does. Standing the plate on its Z end would create the overhangs the current ceiling report assumes.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/nameplate/nameplate-001.step
