[thin] Required First Edition graphic outlines: finite identification strokes begin at 0.325 mm; the frame and divider are 0.42 mm wide, and QR modules are 1.20 mm. The 0.003 mm, zero-area sample is a narrowing at a glyph curve junction, not a continuous membrane. These points belong to the specified raised lettering, QR and frame; this new artwork has CAD validation and no physical print acceptance.
alternatives: Heavier glyphs or larger lettering change the approved type or its balanced layout. A wider frame changes the requested fine border. Larger QR modules increase its footprint; flush ink removes the required relief. Use a variable-width print process for the 0.325 mm identification strokes.
